      "body": "## Motivation\n\nGemma4 tool calls currently turn bare `null` and exponent-form numbers such as `1e-05` into JSON strings. This breaks numeric/nullable tool schemas in both streaming and non-streaming responses.\n\nCloses #41316.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Parse bare `null` as JSON null and `e`/`E` exponent notation as numbers.\n- Preserve integers, booleans, decimal numbers, delimited strings, and malformed bare-string fallback behavior.\n- Extend the existing Gemma4 detector tests with nested values and non-streaming plus streamed chunks of one character, seven characters, and the complete message.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn macOS arm64, Python 3.12.9, Torch 2.14.1, Transformers 5.17.0, and xgrammar 0.2.7:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 \\\n  python -m pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py -q\n```\n\n**251 tests and 59 subtests passed**, including all 18 Gemma4 tests. The new regression fails all eight subcases before the production fix and passes afterward. Applicable pre-commit hooks and `git diff --check` passed. Changed executable-line coverage is **100% (3/3)**, exceeding the repository's 60% threshold.\n\nValidation uses the real detector and protocol classes. Only tokenizer artifacts were downloaded for adjacent DeepSeek fixtures; no model weights, GPU, or inference server was needed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo model or kernel changes and no inference-speed claim. This corrects tool-argument parsing.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format changed files with applicable pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] Add a regression in the existing registered CPU suite and verify it fails before the fix.\n- [x] Document the corrected contract in the regression; no new user-facing option.\n- [x] Record parser validation; model accuracy and inference benchmarking are not applicable.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style.\n\n## Related Work\n\nThe earlier #41319 addressed the same issue and is closed unmerged. This patch was independently implemented on current main; no code was copied from that PR.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\nReady for review. Upstream CI and maintainer approval remain pending.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37268350550](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37268350550)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37268350181](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37268350181)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37268350434](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37268350434)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
